  because a z-index on a static element is inert, which is the shape this bug
  would take again if the position were dropped. Second, the instrument strip
  set overflow: hidden, and a clipping ancestor trims an absolutely positioned
  descendant away whatever z-index that descendant declares -- so each
  instrument's disclosure panel, which hangs below the bar at z-index 40, was
  drawn and then cut off and its button could not be reached. The clip is gone
  and the row is held inside its grid track where it belongs, by each value
  ellipsizing itself. That was already the intent: contextValueClass declared
  text-overflow: ellipsis but also flex-shrink: 0, and a flex item additionally
  defaults to min-width auto, so the ellipsis could never engage and clipping
  from above was the only thing keeping the row in. The value now shrinks, and
  the label span carries the truncation while the chevron does not, because a
  disclosure whose marker is the first thing dropped stops reading as one. The
