Dev-Log: DL-20260802-012
Date: 2026-08-02
Status: Recorded spend is readable, sliced by atoms, molecules, and program
Change-ID: None until a commit is authorized
Request-or-TODO: User: "implement this is the backend and hook it up to the
  front end client, I also want per atom, per molecule and per program costs
  even if its an approximation". Builds on DL-20260802-008
Goal: Expose what recorded work cost and where the money went, from the ledger
  through a read RPC to the settings sheet
Assumptions: A window with no provider call is exactly zero spend. Phases are
  the flow's own seven movements rather than a coarser three, because control
  flow and verification consume real model time and folding them into "program"
  would report assembly as expensive when the checking was
Decisions: Provider calls do not record the stage that made them, so per-phase
  cost is an approximation, and it is labelled as one in the type, in the proto
  field, and on screen. PIPE-006 is still open, so a stage record writes one
  timestamp into both its start and finish columns; interval containment would
  therefore match nothing. The rule instead attributes a call to the first stage
  whose record was written at or after it -- the next stage to finish, which is
  the stage that was running -- and it becomes true containment once PIPE-006
  lands. The stage is found with a correlated scalar subquery, not a join, so a
  call can match at most one stage however the timestamps fall; a join would
  double-count a call that two stage rows both claimed. Totals are summed from
  the calls themselves and never from the phases, so unattributed spend is
  missing from the breakdown but never from the total, and the remainder is
  reported as its own row rather than left as an unexplained gap. Exact cost is
  summed by grouping on (currency, denominator) in SQL and accumulating big.Rat
  in Go, so the number of rational additions is the number of distinct prices
  rather than the number of calls. Money crosses the wire as conventions.proto
  Money at six extra decimal places with an exact flag: this repository already
  interprets decimal_places relative to minor units, whole minor units would
  round most single calls to free, and a rounded figure that claimed to be exact
  is the failure the whole surface exists to prevent. Unknown cost is an absent
  Money and renders "not priced", never a zero
