  points in the stream lifecycle -- so no new ledger was designed. The defect is
  that CostMetrics reads usage_records and model_requests from migration 000001,
  which have zero writers anywhere in the repository; the metric therefore
  returned a confident zero for every window while real spend accumulated in
  provider_attempt_accounting. Repointed the query rather than backfilling the
  dead tables, because usage_records.cost_minor is a whole-minor-unit integer
  and a single call routinely costs a fraction of one minor unit, so that column
  rounds most individual calls to free; the 000009 numerator/denominator pair is
  exact. Left the dead tables in place: dropping them needs a forward migration
  and schema_test.go asserts usage_records exists, which is separable work.
