  four sources per attempt (estimated, provider-partial, provider-final,
  reconciled), so the query takes the highest sequence per attempt; summing
  every row would multiply-count usage by up to four. Exact cost is summed by
  grouping on (currency, denominator) in SQL and accumulating big.Rat in Go,
  which is exact and bounded by the number of distinct denominators rather than
  by the number of calls. Kept CostMinorUnits as a Count so the scorecard's
  regression comparison and surprise check stay untouched, and added KnownCost
  as the exact authoritative figure. Mixed currencies in one window now report
