Goal: Answer whether FTS5 is available here and, if it is, make the atom search
  reach the documented promises instead of only the declaration names
Assumptions: modernc.org/sqlite is the driver everywhere in this product, so
  whether FTS5 exists is a property of that build rather than of a registration
  the caller performs
Decisions: Verified FTS5 is compiled into modernc.org/sqlite v1.55.0 -- the
  ENABLE_FTS5 compile option is present and a virtual table, a MATCH query, and
  a prefix query all work with no registration. Built the index in memory
  beside the parsed repository map rather than in the coordinator's database:
  atoms are derived from the working tree at an exact revision and are already
  recomputed when that revision moves, so persisting them would create a second
  account of what the code says and the two would eventually disagree. Indexed
  each atom's name both whole and split at its case boundaries, because FTS5
  reads a Go identifier as one token and nobody searching for "checkout" types
  ReserveStockUntilCheckoutExpires. Ranked with bm25 weighted toward the name.
  Kept the old substring match as the fallback, so a mid-token query still
  finds what it always found. Quoted and prefixed every typed term, so nothing
  a person types can be read as FTS5 syntax.
